-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 6 recordings (c1, b2, b1, u2, u3, d1), 25,117
              frames, in 4 states (colour, colour + Smooth scrolling,
              monochrome, monochrome + Smooth scrolling): registers with R and
              all game memory equal at every hook event; per state t_isr
              23,989, t_prn 10,584, t_spr 5,181, t_dly 4,848, t_list 1,637
              (+3,528 nested in t_bs), t_c05a 100, t_bs 82, t_paste 56, t_clr
              56, t_sl 35, t_sd 32, t_cls 15, t_su 8, t_sr 7: every hook ran
              (d1, a test recording, has the down-scroll edge lowered from
              line 151 to 112 in its own first snapshot, and the power cheat,
              so that t_su runs). Negatives detected: ink pass skipped, paste
              at the wrong origin, t_dly R delta off by one, sprites not moved
              with the glide, a forced 3.5 MHz exit, the E656 pace window's R
              delta off by one (both states), the monochrome gate dropped; in
              JNext the limiter removed (no debt kept, no window waits) plays
              busy scenes -3.9% (2 trials)

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, v2.09 card: play reached in colour in
              both menu states; nexclash.flicker 300 frames in each state, no
              figure vanished, no one-frame transients, 2 and 1 frames flagged
              out of step against the ULA play area, which Layer 2 hides
              (looked at: the figures whole in every flagged frame);
              nexclash.soak 15 emulated minutes in each state against the
              original, no freeze, loop or crash; both trainers proven in
              session 2

  Coverage    Bot recordings only, no human play: green, white, yellow and
              cyan decks, all four scroll moves in lockstep (t_sd, t_sl, t_sr
              from play; t_su only in the test recording d1), droid classes in
              play X, U, R, B, L; not reached: lifts, transfer game, later
              decks

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
